WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.826
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:09.826
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:16.145
Unit five: Modal Verbs (can/must/should). Today you will talk about ability, obligation and advice.

4
00:00:16.445 --> 00:00:19.098
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.464
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.132
Can.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:29.080
Can means to be able to do something or to have permission.

8
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:30.870
I can swim.

9
00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:33.996
Your turn. Say: Can.

10
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:37.625
Can.

11
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.164
Must.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.660
Must means to have a strong obligation.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.843
You must wear a helmet.

14
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.638
Your turn. Say: Must.

15
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.269
Must.

16
00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:52.820
Should.

17
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:56.942
Should means to give advice or say what is a good idea.

18
00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.062
You should sleep early.

19
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.000
Your turn. Say: Should.

20
00:01:04.867 --> 00:01:05.670
Should.

21
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:07.429
Ability.

22
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:10.881
Ability means the skill to do something.

23
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:13.413
Ability grows with practice.

24
00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:16.530
Your turn. Say: Ability.

25
00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.310
Ability.

26
00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:22.156
Obligation.

27
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.730
Obligation means something you have to do.

28
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:28.270
Paying tax is an obligation.

29
00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:31.489
Your turn. Say: Obligation.

30
00:01:34.333 --> 00:01:35.532
Obligation.

31
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:37.342
Advice.

32
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:41.046
Advice means a suggestion about what to do.

33
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.777
My teacher gave me good advice.

34
00:01:44.383 --> 00:01:46.978
Your turn. Say: Advice.

35
00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:50.962
Advice.

36
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:52.729
Permission.

37
00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:56.262
Permission means a yes from someone in charge.

38
00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.257
I asked for permission.

39
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:01.247
Your turn. Say: Permission.

40
00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.020
Permission.

41
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:06.796
Necessary.

42
00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:10.712
Necessary means needed; you cannot avoid it.

43
00:02:11.317 --> 00:02:13.258
A passport is necessary.

44
00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.108
Your turn. Say: Necessary.

45
00:02:18.967 --> 00:02:20.119
Necessary.

46
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:24.387
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:30.422
Visal, a teacher says 'You must wear a uniform' and 'You should study more'. What is the difference?

48
00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:41.605
Must is a strong rule or obligation. Should is only advice. Can shows ability or permission: I can swim. Can I leave?

49
00:02:42.717 --> 00:02:44.414
How do we use the verb after them?

50
00:02:45.517 --> 00:02:57.367
Always the base verb: She can swim, not she can swims. It stays the same for every subject. For questions, we put the modal first: Can you swim?

51
00:02:58.483 --> 00:02:59.844
What about negatives?

52
00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:11.421
Can't means not able. Mustn't means it is forbidden. Shouldn't means it is not a good idea. Notice mustn't is very strong: you mustn't smoke here.

53
00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.044
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.883 --> 00:03:19.042
Grammar focus: Modals: can and must and should plus base verb.

55
00:03:19.342 --> 00:03:20.657
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.013
I can swim very well.

57
00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:25.556
You must wear a helmet.

58
00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.032
You should sleep early.

59
00:03:28.967 --> 00:03:37.505
Can = ability or permission, must = strong obligation, should = advice. Modals take the base verb and never add s.

60
00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.413
Be careful! Don't say: She can sings very well.

61
00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.343
Say: She can sing very well.

62
00:03:45.643 --> 00:03:47.747
Use the base verb after can.

63
00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:51.035
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:53.334
Rules and Advice.

65
00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:56.353
You must wear a helmet when you ride a motorbike.

66
00:03:57.367 --> 00:03:59.784
You can park here, but you mustn't stay long.

67
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.496
You should drink more water, because it is healthy.

68
00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.034
Students must arrive before eight o'clock.

69
00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.892
Good advice is necessary, and it can change a life.

70
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.920
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:16.783 --> 00:04:19.633
You blank wear a seat belt. It is the law.

72
00:04:19.933 --> 00:04:23.343
A, can. B, must. C, should.

73
00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.760
The answer is B: must.

74
00:04:29.917 --> 00:04:32.952
You blank eat more fruit. It is a good idea.

75
00:04:33.252 --> 00:04:36.302
A, must. B, can. C, should.

76
00:04:39.867 --> 00:04:41.866
The answer is C: should.

77
00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:45.948
I blank speak two languages. (ability)

78
00:04:46.248 --> 00:04:49.181
A, must. B, can. C, should.

79
00:04:52.733 --> 00:04:54.501
The answer is B: can.

80
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.324
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:57.624 --> 00:05:02.218
A, She can sings.. B, She can sing.. C, She cans sing..

82
00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.801
The answer is B: She can sing..

83
00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.623
According to the reading, when must students arrive?

84
00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:15.553
A, before eight. B, after nine. C, at noon.

85
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.680
The answer is A: before eight.

86
00:05:22.867 --> 00:05:26.041
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:26.883 --> 00:05:29.208
Give one piece of advice using 'should'.

88
00:05:38.017 --> 00:05:39.563
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:39.863 --> 00:05:52.053
You should drink more water every day. Water keeps your body healthy and helps you concentrate. I use should because it is advice, not a rule. After should, I use the base verb.

90
00:05:52.353 --> 00:05:53.842
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:54.750 --> 00:06:00.816
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modals: can and must and should plus base verb.

92
00:06:01.116 --> 00:06:05.927
Today's value is wisdom. Think carefully and listen to good advice before you decide.

93
00:06:06.227 --> 00:06:08.706
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:09.006 --> 00:06:11.565
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

